{"step_index":185,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-07T06:15:00Z","input_tokens":2764,"cache_read_tokens":177290,"output_tokens":2763,"tool_calls":[{"name":"write_file","args":{"Content":"# 🛡️ AegisShield EDR - Cyber Process Monitor & Threat Eradicator\n\n> **Advanced Real-Time Spyware, Antivirus, Remote Desktop Control (LOLRMM), Process Monitor, Network Origin Tracer, Access Control & Trojan Detection Dashboard**\n> *Scans your system, identifies threats via multi-vector heuristics and threat intelligence, audits network connections, enforces allow/block rules, dispatches email reports, and kills threats with a single click.*\n\n---\n\n## 🌟 Key Features\n\n### 1. 🛡️ Access Control & Allow / Block Policy Engine\n* **Allowlist (Whitelist):** Explicitly trust processes by **Name**, **Executable Path**, or **SHA256 Hash**. Whitelisted software is assigned a Threat Score of 0, alerts are suppressed, and it is exempt from termination.\n* **Blocklist (Blacklist):** Ban known malicious processes or scripts. Any process matching a blacklist rule is flagged as `CRITICAL` (Score: 100) and can be immediately eradicated.\n* **IP Banning & Windows Firewall Integration:** Ban suspicious remote IP addresses. AegisShield creates outbound rules in Windows Firewall (`netsh advfirewall firewall add rule ...`) and flags any process attempting communication with banned IPs.\n* **Quick UI Actions:** 1-click **Allow** and **Block** buttons located on every process row and threat card.\n\n### 2. 🌐 Network Radar & IP Origin Tracer\n* **Network Process Auditing:** Discovers exactly which processes are using network sockets, mapping local ports to remote IP endpoints.\n* **Origin & Geolocation Tracing:** Resolves remote IPs using reverse DNS (PTR records) and geographic lookup (Country, Organization, ISP, and ASN).\n* **Genuineness & Reputation Classification:** Automatically assesses whether an endpoint is legitimate:\n  * 🟢 **`GENUINE CLOUD / CDN`**: Verified major tech infrastructure (Microsoft/Azure, Google/GCP, Cloudflare, Amazon AWS, Apple, Akamai, GitHub, Fastly).\n  * 🔵 **`PRIVATE LAN`**: Safe local subnet (`192.168.x.x`, `10.x.x.x`, `172.16-31.x.x`, `127.0.0.1`).\n  * 🔴 **`SUSPICIOUS C2 / RAT PORT`**: Communication on known Trojan/RAT ports (`1177`, `1604`, `2404`, `4444`, `4782`, `5555`, `6606`, etc.) or cryptocurrency mining pools.\n  * ⚪ **`UNVERIFIED EXTERNAL`**: General public internet hosts requiring administrative scrutiny.\n* **Interactive Actions:** One-click `Block IP` (Windows Firewall rule) and `Deep Trace` drawer for full ASN & network telemetry.\n\n### 3. 📧 Automated & On-Demand Email Security Reports\n* **Configurable SMTP Dispatch:** Supports Gmail (App Passwords), Outlook, Microsoft 365, or custom corporate SMTP relays with TLS / SSL encryption.\n* **Executive HTML Security Reports:** Formats rich, styled HTML reports including:\n  * Health index, scan timestamp, and host metrics.\n  * Detected threats table with triggered heuristic vectors and risk scores.\n  * Active Remote Desktop / RMM session table.\n  * Network process telemetry and remote IP origin audit.\n  * Incident remediation history (processes terminated and quarantined).\n* **Automated Critical Alerts:** Configurable trigger to automatically dispatch an email when **CRITICAL** threats or unauthorized RAT beacons are detected.\n* **Instant Dispatch:** \"Email Report\" button in the dashboard and CLI (`--email-report`).\n\n### 4. 🕵️ Spyware & Infostealer Detection\n* **Keylogger & Hook Inspection:** Scans binary imports and memory hooks for keystroke logging (`SetWindowsHookEx`, `GetAsyncKeyState`, `GetKeyboardState`).\n* **Screen Scraping & Surveillance:** Detects hidden screen recording APIs (`BitBlt`, `GetDC`) and unauthorized background input capture.\n* **Infostealer Heuristics:** Matches signatures of notorious credential stealers like **AgentTesla**, **RedLine**, **Vidar**, and LSASS dumpers like **Mimikatz**.\n\n### 5. 🦠 Antivirus & Malware Engine\n* **Pure-Python PE Header Inspection:** Extracts COFF headers, architecture, and section structures without requiring external C extensions.\n* **Shannon Entropy Analysis:** Identifies crypted, packed, or UPX-obfuscated executables (Entropy > 7.15).\n* **System Process Masquerading:** Flags processes masquerading as Windows system binaries (e.g. `svchost.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `csrss.exe`) running outside `C:\\Windows\\System32`.\n* **Typosquatting Detection:** Detects deceptive names like `svch0st.exe`, `lsasss.exe`, `scvhost.exe`, `taskmngr.exe`, and `dwm0.exe`.\n* **Suspicious Drop Zones:** Identifies executables executing out of `%TEMP%`, `Users\\Public`, `Downloads`, or the Recycle Bin.\n* **LOLBins Heuristics:** Catches encoded PowerShell (`-enc`, `-encodedcommand`), hidden windows (`-w hidden`), download cradles (`IEX Net.WebClient`), `certutil` downloaders, and ransomware volume shadow deletion (`vssadmin delete shadows`).\n\n### 6. 📡 Remote Desktop & RMM Detector (LOLRMM)\n* **Living Off The Land RMM Tracking:** Automatically discovers 60+ dual-use commercial & open-source remote access tools:\n  * **AnyDesk** (Port 7070, 6568)\n  * **TeamViewer** (Port 5938)\n  * **RustDesk** (Ports 21115 - 21119)\n  * **ConnectWise ScreenConnect** (Ports 8040, 8041)\n  * **VNC Servers** (UltraVNC, RealVNC, TightVNC on ports 5900 - 5905)\n  * **Splashtop**, **LogMeIn**, **Atera**, **NinjaRMM**, **NetSupport Manager**, **Ammyy Admin**, and **Remote Utilities**.\n* **Reverse Tunnels & C2 Proxies:** Detects persistent reverse tunnels often abused by attackers (**Ngrok**, **Cloudflared**, **FRP**, **Chisel**, **Ligolo**).\n\n### 7. ⚡ Threat Eradication (\"Finds it and Kills it\")\n* **Instant Process Termination:** Forcefully terminates rogue processes (`proc.kill()`).\n* **Recursive Tree Eradication:** Kills parent processes and all spawned child processes to prevent surviving beacons.\n* **🚨 Emergency Bulk Kill:** Single-click eradication for all detected threats matching or exceeding threat thresholds.\n* **Core OS Protection Whitelist:** Automatically protects critical Windows OS components (`smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `lsass.exe`, `services.exe` in `C:\\Windows\\System32`) from accidental termination.\n* **Threat Quarantine:** Isolates suspicious binaries into `quarantine/` with execution rights revoked and forensic receipts.\n* **Persistence Neutralization:** Scans and disables malicious autorun items in Windows Startup folders, Registry Run keys (`HKCU`/`HKLM`), and Scheduled Tasks.\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 Quick Start Guide\n\n### Option 1: Double-Click Launcher (Windows)\nDouble-click:\n```bat\nstart_dashboard.bat\n```\nThis automatically starts the backend server and launches the Web Dashboard at:\n👉 **`http://127.0.0.1:8888`**\n\n---\n\n### Option 2: Command Line (CLI)\n\n#### 1. Start Web Dashboard\n```bash\npython run_server.py\n```\n\n#### 2. Terminal CLI Scanner\n```bash\n# 1. Run deep process threat scan\npython cli_scanner.py --scan\n\n# 2. Deep scan and automatically kill all detected threats\npython cli_scanner.py --scan --kill\n\n# 3. Audit processes using network sockets and trace IP origins\npython cli_scanner.py --network\n\n# 4. View active allowlist and blocklist rules\npython cli_scanner.py --rules\n\n# 5. Whitelist (allow) a trusted process\npython cli_scanner.py --allow internal_admin.exe\n\n# 6. Blacklist (ban) a malicious process or remote IP\npython cli_scanner.py --block bad_tool.exe\npython cli_scanner.py --block 198.51.100.50\n\n# 7. Generate and send full HTML security report to email\npython cli_scanner.py --email-report admin@yourdomain.com\n\n# 8. Check specifically for Remote Desktop / RMM / VNC sessions\npython cli_scanner.py --rmm\n\n# 9. Forcefully terminate a specific PID or entire process tree\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-pid 1234\npython cli_scanner.py --kill-tree 1234\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📁 File Structure\n\n```\nSpywareProcessMon/\n├── backend/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── config.py              # Configuration, whitelists, critical binaries, ports\n│   ├── policy_engine.py       # Allowlist, blocklist & Windows Firewall rules engine\n│   ├── network_tracer.py      # Network process auditor, reverse DNS, GeoIP & Genuineness scorer\n│   ├── email_notifier.py      # SMTP dispatcher & HTML threat report generator\n│   ├── signatures_db.py       # Catalog of LOLRMM tools, RATs, infostealers, heuristics\n│   ├── pe_analyzer.py         # Pure-Python PE parser, Shannon entropy, API string scanner\n│   ├── network_monitor.py     # Sockets, listening ports, remote connections, RMM ports\n│   ├── persistence_hunter.py  # Startup folders, Registry Run keys, Scheduled Tasks\n│   ├── detector.py            # Multi-vector detection engine (8 analysis passes)\n│   ├── remediator.py          # Kill engine, process tree terminator, quarantine, audit log\n│   ├── simulator.py           # Benign threat simulation test suite\n│   └── server.py              # FastAPI REST API + WebSockets telemetry server\n├── database/\n│   ├── policy_rules.json      # Persistent whitelist and blacklist rules\n│   ├── email_config.json      # SMTP server configuration\n│   └── geo_cache.json         # Cached IP intelligence lookups\n├── frontend/\n│   ├── index.html             # Cyber SOC Dashboard UI\n│   ├── css/\n│   │   └── dashboard.css      # Dark SOC cyber styling, animations, glow effects\n│   └── js/\n│       └── app.js             # Real-time WebSocket/polling, state management, audio chimes\n├── cli_scanner.py             # CLI tool for terminal scans, kills, and network tracing\n├── run_server.py              # Server launcher script with automatic browser open\n├── start_dashboard.bat        # Windows 1-click batch launcher\n├── requirements.txt           # Python dependencies (fastapi, uvicorn, psutil, requests)\n└── README.md                  # Complete documentation\n```\n\n---\n\n## 🔒 Security & Safety Controls\n1. **Critical System Whitelist:** Protected system processes (`system`, `registry`, `smss.exe`, `csrss.exe`, `wininit.exe`, `services.exe`, `lsass.exe`) running from verified `System32` paths cannot be terminated.\n2. **Access Control Overrides:** Whitelisted software cannot be flagged or terminated by automated scans.\n3. **Audit Trail:** Every scan, process termination, tree kill, quarantine, and email dispatch is logged in `logs/audit_events.json` and exportable as JSON.\n","Overwrite":true,"Path":"c:\\Users\\thann\\Downloads\\AntiGravity\\SpywareProcessMon\\README.md"}}]}
