tion\"**.\n5. **Quick Allow / Block:** In the **Process Explorer** and **Threat Center**, click **\"Allow\"** to instantly whitelist a process or **\"Block\"** to ban it.\n\n#### From the Terminal (CLI):\n```bash\n# 1. Audit all processes using the network and trace IP origin\npython cli_scanner.py --network\n\n# 2. View all active allowlist and blocklist rules\npython cli_scanner.py --rules\n\n# 3. Whitelist (trust) a process\npython cli_scanner.py --allow internal_admin.exe\n\n# 4. Blacklist (ban) a process or remote IP\npython cli_scanner.py --block bad_tool.exe\npython cli_scanner.py --block 198.51.100.50\n\n# 5. Generate and dispatch full HTML security report to an email\npython cli_scanner.py --email-report admin@yourdomain.com\n```","thinking":"Initial analysis focuses on the policy engine and network tracer modules. The policy engine defines whitelists and blacklists to control process execution and network access. The network tracer audits network activity, mapping ports to endpoints, and classifying connections based on their nature. This suggests the system is designed for security monitoring and control.\n\n\n"}
